 "claim_limits": [
  "A static decode and a content join, not a captured frame: the receipt marks the Handler rule as conditional on runtime enable and context, so a Header here is eligible, not proven drawn.",
  "Only the cars with an aligned draw are listed; any other car or part renders unchanged.",
  "The preview is capture-time GS memory at the sampled address (view-render-target-0), not the post-render contents at the aligned draw. It is a stand-in for the sampled texture.",
  "The eye position and the 3x3 matrix are not in the receipt; the inspector uses the camera as the eye and a view-derived matrix, and labels the result candidate.",
  "The capture comparison verifies the pass-5 per-draw RGBA relation and the STQ T lane on 63 draws, not S: the specular intensity is a static reading of the decoded arithmetic, and the sampled specular texture function is not in the receipt.",
  "The pass-5 light inputs (DM[5], DM[6]) come from game state; the inspector substitutes the retained capture values as fixed stand-ins, so a listed Header is eligible for the highlight, not shown with the game's own light."
 ]
